      "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #45226.\n\nIn the qwen3_coder streaming detector, a model that repeats the closers after a complete call (the `</invoke></function></tool_call>` tail from the issue's shape A) hit the `</function>` branch with no function open (`current_func_name` was cleared when the call closed) and got a second `}` appended into the finished call's arguments — `{\"ref\": \"p9\"}}`, invalid JSON. Each stray `</function>` added one more.\n\nThe branch now only emits the closing brace when a function is actually open; a stray `</function>` is consumed without output, matching the one-shot `detect_and_parse` behavior the issue measured. The empty-parameters path (`<function=name>` straight into `</function>`) is unchanged — the function is open there, so `{}` is still emitted correctly.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- New regression test `test_streaming_stray_closing_tags_do_not_corrupt_arguments` (the issue's shape A as chunked streaming input): the finished call's arguments stay valid JSON.\n- `pytest test/registered/function_call/test_function_call_parser.py -k Qwen3Coder`: 14 passed (CPU, local).\n- Mutation check: with the guard removed the new test fails on the invalid JSON (restored green).\n- Full file: 139 passed + 7 pre-existing `TestDeepSeekV32Detector` failures that fail identically on unmodified main in this environment (no GPU here), so they are not from this change.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39765971190](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39765971190)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39765971022](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39765971022)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39765971069](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39765971069)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
