    {
      "body": "Rebased onto current main (8dc7f98005); new head daf31e5211.\n\nGitHub had the PR dirty, but the pick applied cleanly: the conflict was positional, because the parser test file moved to `test/registered/unit/function_call/` in #20631. The change now lands on the moved path, and the anyOf/allOf argument-resolution work that landed since the base is on a different seam from the stray-closing-tag guard, so the two compose.\n\nVerified: `test/registered/unit/function_call/test_function_call_parser.py` 256 passed / 485 subtests on the new head; the new `test_streaming_stray_closing_tags_do_not_corrupt_arguments` fails on bare 8dc7f98005 with the unpatched detector, so it pins the fix exactly. CPU-only env, no GPU run.",
